ng and Telecom clients in the UK\n• Architected migration of Conversational AI platforms from IBM Cloud to Azure using NLP frameworks and cloud re-engineering, \nimproving reliability, performance, and cost efficiency with minimal downtime.\n• Collaborated with business, vendor, and technical stakeholders to define architecture blueprints, delivery plans, and execution \ngovernance, ensuring program stability, stakeholder alignment, and successful deployment.\nUniphore\nSenior Software Engineer\nBengaluru, India · Nov 2018 - Aug 2019\n• Built advanced NLP and conversational AI solutions for healthcare client using deep learning (Bi-LSTM, entity extraction) deployed \nin secure cloud environments, enabling automation, improved service quality, and operational efficiency.\n• Led secure deployment and lifecycle management of ML/DL models, ensuring reliability, compliance, and sustained performance.\nPlankton Solutions\nSenior Software Engineer\nBengaluru, India · Jun 2016 - Nov 2018\n• Designed and deployed enterprise chatbot and analytics platforms using AI/ML and AWS cloud infrastructure, enhancing customer \nexperience and operational intelligence.\n• Led presales engineering and created client solutions using Salesforce and Azure, built REST APIs with Flask, and delivered analytics \ndashboards, which accelerated client adoption of the AI product and ensured the solution met market requirements\nTech Mahindra\nSenior Project Engineer\nBengaluru, India · Jan 2014 - Jun 2016\n• Delivered enterprise automation solutions across QA, UI, and reporting for Fortune 500 clients using Python, Selenium, Appium tools, \nimproving operational efficiency, stability, and risk governance.\nCERTIFICATION\n• Agentic AI - DeepLearning.AI\n• Generative AI Engineer Associate - Databricks\n• Google Cloud GenAI Level 3 - Wipro AI Academy\n• AI Product Management - Duke University\n• Project Management - Google\n• Azure AI Developer Associate - Microsoft\n• Azure AI Fundamentals - Microsoft\nSKILLS\n• AI/ML: Azure OpenAI, AWS Bedrock, Google Vertex AI, Databricks, Agentspace, LangChain, AutoGen, RAG architectures, \nMulti-agent systems, MLOps (Azure ML, MLflow), Conversational AI, NLP\n• Cloud & Data: Azure, AWS, Google Cloud, Snowflake, Vector DBs (Pinecone, Milvus. ChromaDB)\n• Software Development: Python, Langchain, REST APIs (Flask/FastAPI), JavaScript, Docker, CI/CD, Git\n• Enterprise Platforms: Salesforce, MS Dynamics 365, Facets, NICE CXone, Coupa, SAP Ariba, Oracle Cloud ERP, Workday\n• Methodologies & Compliance: Agile/Scrum, Product Management, AI Governance, Responsible AI, HIPAA/GDPR, Data-Driven \nDecision Making, Customer Insights\n• Industry Domains: Healthcare & Life Sciences, Energy & Utilities, Consumer Retail, E-commerce AI, Enterprise Knowledge \nManagement, Contact Center Transformation\nPROJECTS\nmulti-agent Financial Analysis system\n• Developed a multi-agent Financial Analysis system using Ollama (local LLMs), LangChain with hybrid RAG retrieval, implemented \nPlanner, Research, and Reporting agents that parse earnings transcripts, extract financial metrics from SEC Edgar filings, benchmark \nagainst competitor data, and autonomously generate executive summaries with actionable recommendations validated across 15 \ncompany analyses.\nRAG-powered Knowledge Copilot\n• Built a RAG-powered Knowledge Copilot using open-source LLMs, ChromaDB, LangChain, FastAPI, and Python to process complex \nenterprise documentation including SOPs, policies, and compliance rules; implemented multi-stage retrieval with semantic reranking, \nanswer grounding with source citations, and structured reasoning chains achieving 82% answer accuracy on internal knowledge base \nevaluation set and enabling self-service knowledge access for operational teams.\nAutonomous Resume Intelligence & ATS Scoring system\n• Built an Autonomous Resume Intelligence & ATS Scoring system using open-source LLMs (Ollama), sentence-transformer embed-\ndings, Milvus, LangGraph, and Python; designed multi-agent pipeline with Parsing, JD Matching, Skills Gap Analysis, and ATS \nCompliance agents that extract structured resume data, compute semantic similarity against job descriptions, perform keyword-based \nATS scoring, identify missing qualifications, and generate improvement recommendation tested across 50+ resume-JD pairs with 85% \nalignment to recruiter assessments.\n\n        \n        Analyze the resume against the JD. Provide a JSON response with the following structure:\n        {\n            "match_score": <int 0-100>,\n            "swot_analysis": {\n                "strengths": ["list of strings"],\n                "weaknesses": ["list of strings"],\n                "opportunities": ["list of strings"],\n                "threats": ["list of strings"]\n            },\n            "recommendations": [\n                {\n                    "original": "<exact sentence from resume>",\n                    "suggested": "<rewritten sentence optimized for ATS and impact>",\n                    "reason": "<brief explanation>"\n                }\n            ]\n        }\n        Return ONLY valid JSON. Do not add markdown formatting like ```json.\n        '}], 'model': 'llama-3.3-70b-versatile', 'response_format': {'type': 'json_object'}, 'temperature': 0.0}}
