et requirements."\nYOUR REWRITE: "Facilitated requirements gathering workshops with 10+ cross-functional stakeholders using Agile methodologies, translating business needs into technical specs that reduced development rework by 15%."\n\n=== END EXAMPLES ===\n\n### INPUT DATA:\nJob Description:\nAbout the job\nTo be a part of a cutting-edge startup revolutionizing mobile app testing.\nOpportunity to jump into real-world challenges from day 1.\n\n\nAbout Our Client\n\nThe client is an AI-first startup focused on transforming mobile app testing through Vision AI, enabling teams to create and run tests using natural language and visual understanding instead of traditional scripts. They\'re backed by top-tier investors and led by experienced engineers from global tech companies.\n\nJob Description\n\nDevelop the road-map and implement AI strategies to achieve business goals.\nLead the design and deployment of AI-driven features.\nIdentify and evaluate emerging AI technologies for potential business applications.\nOversee data collection, processing, and analysis to support AI initiatives.\nEnsure compliance with industry standards and best practices in AI development.\nMentor and grow a team of AI professionals.\nMonitor the performance and effectiveness of AI implementations, suggesting improvements as needed.\n\n\nThe Successful Applicant\n\nA successful Head AI should have:\n\nA strong educational background in computer science, data science, or a related field from preferably a T1 engineering college.\nA minimum of 6 years of experience and no more than 12 years of experience.\nMust have experience in working in Vision language models or Computer Vision.\nProficiency in machine learning algorithms, NLP, and programming languages.\nKnowledge of AI ethics, compliance, and industry standards.\nAbility to identify and implement innovative AI solutions to business challenges.\nAbility to work with cross-functional teams and have demonstrated leadership/mentoring skills.\n\nWhat\'s on Offer\n\nCompetitive salary package.\nOpportunity to lead AI initiatives in a small-sized, innovative organization.\nWork in a dynamic environment in Bengaluru.\nProfessional growth and learning opportunities.\n\nIf you are passionate about Vision Language Models and want to do impactful work, we encourage you to apply for this exciting opportunity in Bengaluru.\n\nResume Content:\nPAVAN HARESH \n+1 214-430-6317| paven026@gmail.com| linkedin.com/in/impavan/| Texas| USA(Open to Relocate) \n \nPROFESSIONAL SUMMARY \nAI Strategy and Enterprise Transformation Leader with 12+ years of experience driving large-scale AI adoption, product innovation, and \nmeasurable enterprise value across Healthcare, Retail, BFSI, and Energy verticals and cross industry functions such as F&A, HR, Procurement, \nlegal, marketing, Supply Chain. Proven commercial and delivery track record generating $250M+ pipeline, closing $50M+ revenue, and enabling \n$1B+ in business impact through AI modernization, platform development, and GTM execution. Deep expertise in Generative AI, Agentic AI, RAG \necosystems, Conversational AI, Knowledge Intelligence, and enterprise AI platforms across Azure, AWS, and Google Cloud combining hands-on \ntechnical credibility with strong product leadership and C-Suite partnership. Recognized for building scalable AI platforms, establishing \nresponsible AI governance in regulated environments, and leading cross-functional engineering, data, and product teams to deliver secure, \ncompliant, and high-impact AI solutions at enterprise scale. \n \nEDUCATION \nVisvesvaraya Technological University (VTU) \nBachelor of Engineering, Computer Science   \n \n \n \n \n                                      August 2009 - July 2013 \n \nEXPERIENCE \nWipro \nSenior Product Manager & Practice Partner  \n \n \n \n \n                                  November 2023 - Present \nPlano, TX, USA \n• \nDirected AI strategy and GTM execution across Healthcare, Retail, Life Sciences, Telecom verticals using ML/DL, GenAI, Agentic AI, and \nknowledge intelligence platforms, driving ~$250M opportunity pipeline and ~$50M+ in closed revenue. \n• \nPartnered with C-Suite leadership to build enterprise AI modernization roadmaps spanning clinical operations, regulatory workflows, \nand automation programs, aligning technology investments to measurable business outcomes and scalable value realization. \n• \nEstablished a large-scale AI Center of Excellence for a major U.S. healthcare payer leveraging GenAI, decision intelligence, and \nautomated workflows, reducing manual reviews by ~40%, improving claim turnaround by 25–30%, and delivering $50M+ annual cost \nefficiencies. \n• \nArchitected behavioral claims audit automation with Multi Agent System using Azure, Langchain stack across 5M+ annual claims, \nenabling real-time fraud and compliance anomaly detection and reducing manual intervention while increasing audit accuracy and \noperational assurance. \n• \nBuilt an enterprise Agentic AI system and workflow orchestration POC on Azure/Autogen stack to automate plan build and onboarding \nprocesses, cutting configuration cycles by 60%. \n• \nDesigned GenAI SOP conversational agent on Azure to find accurate answers from relevant SOP clauses, enhancing Dental First pass \nand adjustments claims processor\'s efficiency by 30%. \nProduct Manager \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n                      February 2022 - November 2023 \nLondon, UK \n• \nOwned global product roadmap and delivery for AI-powered Knowledge Platforms built using Azure Cognitive Search (BM25 + \nSemantic + Hybrid Search), indexing 80M+ documents across 12TB of enterprise content and improving knowledge access and \ndecisioning for ENU client. \n• \nLed agile delivery as Product Manager and Scrum Master, managing sprints, stakeholder priorities, and platform enhancements to \nensure predictable delivery, product adoption, and measurable business outcomes. \n• \nOversaw enterprise migration from Apache Solr to Azure Cognitive Search, enhancing scalability, search results relevancy and \naccuracy, improving search efficiency and operational resilience. \n• \nDefined and executed responsible AI governance practices aligned to regulatory frameworks, ensuring secure, compliant, and risk-\naware AI adoption. \n• \nAdvanced GTM execution for AI offerings in regulated industries, guiding customers from PoC to full enterprise rollout, driving tangible \nROI and operational modernization. \n \nSolution Architect \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n        August 2019 - February 2022 \nBengaluru, India \n• \nDesigned and implemented end-to-end architecture and delivery of Contact Center Transformation and Knowledge Intelligence \nplatforms on Azure, aligning technical solutions to business goals, scalability requirements, and security standards for Manufacturing \nand Telecom clients in UK geo. \n• \nArchitected migration of Conversational AI platforms from IBM Cloud to Azure using NLP frameworks and cloud re-engineering, \nimproving reliability, performance, and cost efficiency with minimal downtime. \n• \nCollaborated with business, vendor, and technical stakeholders to define architecture blueprints, delivery plans, and execution \ngovernance, ensuring program stability, stakeholder alignment, and successful deployment. \n \n \n \nUniphore \nSenior Software Engineer  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n                         November 2018 - August 2019 \nBengaluru, India \n• \nBuilt advanced NLP and conversational AI solutions for healthcare client using deep learning (Bi-LSTM, entity extraction) deployed in \nsecure cloud environments, enabling automation, improved service quality, and operational efficiency. \n• \nLed secure deployment and lifecycle management of ML/DL models, ensuring reliability, compliance, and sustained performance. \nPlankton Solutions \nSenior Software Engineer \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n          June 2016 - November 2018 \nBengaluru, India \n• \nDesigned and deployed enterprise chatbot and analytics platforms using AI/ML and AWS cloud infrastructure, enhancing customer \nexperience and operational intelligence. \n• \nLed presales engineering, client solution design, and analytics delivery, supporting successful client adoption and market-\naligned AI deployment. \nTech Mahindra \nSenior Project Engineer \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n               January 2014 - June 2016 \nBengaluru, India \n• \nDelivered enterprise automation solutions across QA, UI, and reporting for Fortune 500 clients using Python, Selenium, Appium tools, \nimproving operational efficiency, stability, and risk governance. \n \nCERTIFICATION \n• \nAgentic AI - DeepLearning.AI \n• \nGenerative AI Engineer Associate - Databricks \n• \nGoogle Cloud GenAI Level 3 - Wipro AI Academy \n• \nAI Product Management - Duke University \n• \nProject Management - Google \n• \nAzure AI Developer Associate - Microsoft \n• \nAzure AI Fundamentals - Microsoft \n \nSKILLS \n• \nAI/ML: Azure OpenAI, AWS Bedrock, Google Vertex AI, Databricks, Agentspace, LangChain, AutoGen, RAG architectures, Multi-agent \nsystems, MLOps (Azure ML, MLflow) \n• \nCloud & Data: Azure, AWS, Google Cloud, Snowflake, Vector DBs (Pinecone, Milvus. ChromaDB) \n• \nSoftware Development: Python, Langchain, REST APIs (Flask/FastAPI), JavaScript, Docker, CI/CD, Git \n• \nEnterprise Platforms: Salesforce, MS Dynamics 365, Facets, NICE CXone, Coupa, SAP Ariba, Oracle Cloud ERP, Workday \n• \nMethodologies & Compliance: Agile/Scrum, Product Management, AI Governance, Responsible AI, HIPAA/GDPR \n• \nIndustry Domains: Healthcare & Life Sciences, Energy & Utilities, Consumer Retail, E-commerce AI, Enterprise Knowledge \nManagement, Contact Center Transformation \n \nPROJECTS \n• \nDeveloped a multi-agent Financial Analysis system using Ollama (local LLMs), LangChain with hybrid RAG retrieval, implemented \nPlanner, Research, and Reporting agents that parse earnings transcripts, extract financial metrics from SEC Edgar filings, benchmark \nagainst competitor data, and autonomously generate executive summaries with \nactionable recommendations validated across 15 company analyses. \n• \nBuilt a RAG-powered Knowledge Copilot using open-source LLMs, ChromaDB, LangChain, FastAPI, and Python to process complex \nenterprise documentation including SOPs, policies, and compliance rules; implemented multi-stage \nretrieval with semantic reranking, answer grounding with source citations, and structured reasoning chains achieving 82% answer \naccuracy on internal knowledge base evaluation set and enabling self-service knowledge access \nfor operational teams. \n• \nBuilt an Autonomous Resume Intelligence & ATS Scoring system using open-source LLMs (Ollama), sentence-transformer embeddings, \nMilvus, LangGraph, and Python; designed multi-agent pipeline with Parsing, JD Matching, Skills Gap Analysis, and ATS Compliance \nagents that extract structured resume data, compute semantic similarity against job descriptions, perform keyword-based ATS scoring, \nidentify missing qualifications, and generate improvement recommendation tested across 50+ resume-JD pairs with 85% alignment to \nrecruiter assessments. \n\n\n### OUTPUT REQUIREMENT:\nAnalyze the resume against the JD and return a valid JSON response with the following structure:\n{\n    "match_score": <int 0-100>,\n    "swot_analysis": {\n        "strengths": ["list of strings"],\n        "weaknesses": ["list of strings"],\n        "opportunities": ["list of strings"],\n        "threats": ["list of strings"]\n    },\n    "recommendations": [\n        {\n            "original": "<exact sentence from resume>",\n            "suggested": "<rewritten sentence optimized for ATS and impact>",\n            "reason": "<brief explanation>"\n        }\n    ]\n}\n\n**IMPORTANT:** Return ONLY valid JSON. Do not use Markdown formatting (like ```json). Do not add any conversational text.\n'}], 'model': 'llama-3.3-70b-versatile', 'response_format': 