2026-01-14 15:00:24,434 - DEBUG - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/openai/v1/chat/completions', 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-e67bc698-12f4-4199-bf7b-873adb3f62df', 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': '\nYou are an expert Resume ATS Scanner and Career Coach.\n\n### YOUR INSTRUCTIONS:\n1. **Analyze**: Identify critical hard skills, tools, and domain keywords in the JD that are missing or under-emphasized in the Resume.\n2. **Transform**: Rewrite specific bullet points to include these keywords naturally.\n3. **Quantify**: Always add metrics (%, $, time saved) where possible.\n4. **Action Verbs**: Start every bullet with a strong power verb.\n\n### FEW-SHOT TRAINING EXAMPLES (LEARN THIS STYLE):\n\n=== EXAMPLE 1: AI & DATA SCIENCE ===\nJD Requires: "Experience with NLP, Transformers, and deploying models to production."\nOriginal Bullet: "Used machine learning models for text analysis."\nYOUR REWRITE: "Fine-tuned BERT-based Transformer models for NLP sentiment analysis and deployed inference pipelines via Docker, increasing prediction accuracy by 18%."\n\n=== EXAMPLE 2: CYBERSECURITY ===\nJD Requires: "Vulnerability assessment, SIEM tools (Splunk), and NIST compliance."\nOriginal Bullet: "Monitored network security and checked for bugs."\nYOUR REWRITE: "Conducted weekly vulnerability assessments using Nessus and monitored Splunk SIEM logs, reducing mean-time-to-detect (MTTD) threats by 40% in alignment with NIST frameworks."\n\n=== EXAMPLE 3: MAINFRAME ===\nJD Requires: "COBOL, JCL optimization, and DB2."\nOriginal Bullet: "Maintained old code for banking system."\nYOUR REWRITE: "Optimized legacy COBOL batch processing jobs and JCL scripts, reducing nightly batch run-time by 3 hours and ensuring 99.99% uptime for core banking DB2 transactions."\n\n=== EXAMPLE 4: BUSINESS ANALYST ===\nJD Requires: "Stakeholder management, Agile methodologies, and requirements gathering."\nOriginal Bullet: "Talked to clients to get requirements."\nYOUR REWRITE: "Facilitated requirements gathering workshops with 10+ cross-functional stakeholders using Agile methodologies, translating business needs into technical specs that reduced development rework by 15%."\n\n=== END EXAMPLES ===\n\n### INPUT DATA:\nJob Description:\nAI Adoption Lead (Head – AI Adoption Office / AIAO)\n \nLocation: Flexible / Hybrid\nReporting To: Dave Chintan (Executive Sponsor – AIAO)\nStart: Immediate\nScope: Group-wide (All Sarder® Companies as Customer-0)\n \n \n---\n \nRole Summary\n \nThe AI Adoption Lead will own end-to-end execution of AI adoption across all Sarder® businesses, treating the organization as Customer-0. This role is responsible for turning AI from pilots and tools into daily workflows with measurable business impact.\n \nThis is not a research, experimentation, or innovation-lab role. This is an execution, change, and ROI ownership role.\n \n \n---\n \nCore Mandate\n \nDrive fast, disciplined, and measurable AI adoption across all businesses by redesigning workflows, enforcing usage, managing change, and delivering ROI—then converting learnings into scalable playbooks and offerings.\n \n \n---\n \nKey Responsibilities\n \n1. Customer-0 AI Adoption Execution\n \nLead AI adoption across Sales, Marketing, Operations, Finance, HR, Product, and Support\n \nIdentify, prioritize, and sequence high-ROI AI use cases\n \nEnsure AI is embedded into daily workflows (not optional tools)\n \n \n2. Workflow Redesign & Operating Model Change\n \nRedesign existing workflows with AI as a default layer\n \nDefine pre-AI vs post-AI processes\n \nQuantify time saved, cost saved, and revenue impact\n \nEliminate manual handoffs, duplications, and approval bottlenecks\n \n \n3. Change Management & Enablement\n \nDrive behavioral adoption, not just tool deployment\n \nAddress resistance and ensure leadership buy-in\n \nDesign lightweight enablement tied directly to workflows\n \nMake AI usage part of weekly and monthly operating rhythms\n \n \n4. ROI, Metrics & Reporting\n \nDefine success metrics for every AI use case\n \nTrack adoption, usage, and impact weekly\n \nMaintain executive-level dashboards and reviews\n \nOwn success/failure transparently—no vanity metrics\n \n \n5. AIAO Team Leadership\n \nBuild and manage:\n \n2 dedicated AIAO resources\n \nEmbedded BU SMEs (dotted-line)\n \n \nCoordinate cross-functionally with speed and low bureaucracy\n \n \n6. Playbooks & Commercialization\n \nConvert Customer-0 learnings into:\n \nAI adoption playbooks\n \nTemplates, frameworks, SOPs\n \nPackaged offerings (Adoptify AI®)\n \n \nEnsure outputs are repeatable, scalable, and sellable\n \n \n \n---\n \nSuccess Metrics (Indicative)\n \n% of priority workflows AI-enabled\n \nMeasurable time and cost savings per function\n \nRevenue uplift or pipeline efficiency gains\n \nWeekly active AI usage by teams\n \nSpeed from use-case identification to production adoption\n \nNumber of playbooks converted into offerings\n \n \n \n---\n \nRequired Experience\n \nMust-Have\n \n8–15 years in enterprise execution roles\n \nProven experience in:\n \nEnterprise transformation\n \nWorkflow redesign\n \nChange management\n \nLarge-scale system, automation, or AI rollouts\n \n \nStrong business acumen with ownership of ROI and metrics\n \nAbility to influence senior leaders and drive adoption without direct authority\n \n \nStrongly Preferred\n \nBackground in consulting (Big 4 / McKinsey / Accenture or similar) OR\n \nLed internal transformation at a mid-to-large enterprise\n \nExperience rolling out CRM, ERP, RPA, analytics, or AI platforms\n \nPractical exposure to GenAI in business workflows\n \n \n \n---\n \nWhat This Role Is NOT\n \nNot a data scientist role\n \nNot an AI research role\n \nNot an innovation lab or experimentation role\n \nNot a strategy-only role\n \n \nThis role owns execution, adoption, and results.\n \n \n---\n \nTraits That Win in This Role\n \nExecution-obsessed mindset\n \nComfort with ambiguity and speed\n \nClear, direct communicator\n \nOperator mentality (not tool evangelism)\n \nWillingness to challenge priorities and say no\n \n \n \n---\n \nRecruiter Brief (Internal / External)\n \nWhy This Role Exists\n \nSarder® companies are becoming Customer-0 for enterprise AI adoption. We require a senior operator to ensure AI is used daily, workflows are redesigned, and ROI is delivered—not just discussed.\n \nWhat Success Looks Like (Plain English)\n \nAI embedded into daily workflows across functions\n \nManual work eliminated or reduced significantly\n \nTime, cost, and revenue impact measured weekly\n \nAdoption enforced through operating cadence\n \nLearnings converted into repeatable, commercial playbooks\n \n \nIdeal Candidate Profile\n \nTarget backgrounds:\n \nEnterprise transformation leaders\n \nEx-consulting with hands-on execution ownership\n \nOps, RevOps, Automation, or Digital Transformation heads\n \nLeaders who have rolled out systems company-wide and owned outcomes\n \n \nDo NOT send profiles with:\n \nPure data science or research focus\n \nPOC-only or innovation lab backgrounds\n \nTool evangelism without P&L accountability\n \n \nKeywords for Search\n \nEnterprise AI Adoption\n \nDigital Transformation Lead\n \nAutomation / Ops Excellence\n \nChange Management + AI\n \nWorkflow Redesign\n \n \nReporting & Visibility\n \nReports directly to Dave Chintan\n \nHigh-visibility, high-accountability role\n \nDirect impact on operational efficiency and revenue\n \n \n \n---\n \nPre-Interview Execution Task (Mandatory)\n \nShortlisted candidates must complete the following execution-focused task prior to final interview rounds. This task is designed to assess real-world prioritization, execution discipline, and ROI thinking — not AI theory.\n \nTask Objective\n \nDemonstrate how you would drive fast, disciplined, measurable AI adoption by treating the organization as Customer-0.\n \nScenario\n \nYou are joining as AI Adoption Lead for a multi-business group. AI tools exist, but adoption is uneven, inconsistent, and largely unmeasured.\n \nLeadership mandate:\n \n> “Make us Customer-0 for disciplined, ROI-driven AI adoption in 90 days.”\n \n \n \nWhat to Prepare\n \nPrepare either:\n \nA 5–7 slide deck, OR\n \nA 2–3 page execution memo\n \n \nCover the following:\n \n1. First 30 Days – Where Do You Start?\n \nTop 3–5 workflows to target first\n \nClear ROI logic behind each choice\n \nWhat you deliberately will not address initially (and why)\n \n \n2. 90-Day Execution Plan\n \nKey actions for:\n \nDays 1–30\n \nDays 31–60\n \nDays 61–90\n \n \nWhat must be live in production by Day 90\n \n \n3. Adoption Enforcement Model\n \nHow AI usage becomes non-optional\n \nHow resistance is handled (teams and leaders)\n \nOperating cadence introduced (weekly / monthly)\n \n \n4. ROI & Metrics\n \n5–7 hard metrics tracked weekly\n \nHow value is proven to the CEO in 90 days\n \nOne concrete example of time saved, cost reduced, or revenue impacted\n \n \n5. From Customer-0 to Playbooks\n \nHow internal learnings convert into:\n \nRepeatable playbooks\n \nTemplates or SOPs\n \nClient-ready offerings\n \n \n \nConstraints\n \nNo generic AI strategy frameworks\n \nNo vendor-led or tool-centric narratives\n \nAssume limited time, imperfect data, and real resistance\n \nBias toward action over perfection\n \n \nTime Expectation\n \n2–3 hours maximum\n \n \nEvaluation Criteria\n \nExecution and prioritization clarity\n \nChange management realism\n \nROI discipline\n \nCEO-level communication\n \n \n \n---\n \nRecruiter Brief (Internal / External)\n \nWhy This Role Exists\n \nSarder® companies are becoming Customer-0 for enterprise AI adoption. We require a senior operator to ensure AI is embedded into daily workflows, adoption is enforced, and ROI is delivered — not just discussed.\n \nWhat Success Looks Like (Plain English)\n \nAI embedded into daily workflows across functions\n \nManual work eliminated or materially reduced\n \nTime, cost, and revenue impact measured weekly\n \nAdoption enforced through operating cadence\n \nLearnings converted into repeatable, commercial playbooks\n \n \nIdeal Candidate Profile\n \nTarget backgrounds:\n \nEnterprise transformation leaders\n \nEx-consulting professionals with hands-on execution ownership\n \nOps, RevOps, Automation, or Digital Transformation heads\n \nLeaders who have rolled out systems company-wide and owned outcomes\n \n \nDo NOT send profiles with:\n \nPure data science or research focus\n \nPOC-only or innovation lab backgrounds\n \nTool evangelism without P&L accountability\n \n \nKeywords for Search\n \nEnterprise AI Adoption\n \nDigital Transformation Lead\n \nAutomation / Ops Excellence\n \nChange Management + AI\n \nWorkflow Redesign\n \n \nReporting & Visibility\n \nReports directly to Dave Chintan\n \nHigh-visibility, high-accountability role\n \nDirect impact on operational efficiency and revenue\n \n \n \n---\n \nHiring Guidance\n \nPrioritize candidates with execution scars, not frameworks. The right hire will speak in specifics: what broke, how adoption was enforced, and what measurable outcomes were delivered.\n\nResume Content:\nPAVAN HARESH \n+1 214-430-6317| paven026@gmail.com| linkedin.com/in/impavan/| Texas| USA(Open to Relocate) \n \nPROFESSIONAL SUMMARY \nAI Strategy and Enterprise Transformation Leader with 12+ years of experience driving large-scale AI adoption, product innovation, and \nmeasurable enterprise value across Healthcare, Retail, BFSI, and Energy verticals and cross industry functions such as F&A, HR, Procurement, \nlegal, marketing, Supply Chain. Proven commercial and delivery track record generating $250M+ pipeline, closing $50M+ revenue, and enabling \n$1B+ in business impact through AI modernization, platform development, and GTM execution. Deep expertise in Generative AI, Agentic AI, RAG \necosystems, Conversational AI, Knowledge Intelligence, and enterprise AI platforms across Azure, AWS, and Google Cloud combining hands-on \ntechnical credibility with strong product leadership and C-Suite partnership. Recognized for building scalable AI platforms, establishing \nresponsible AI governance in regulated environments, and leading cross-functional engineering, data, and product teams to deliver secure, \ncompliant, and high-impact AI solutions at enterprise scale. \n \nEDUCATION \nVisvesvaraya Technological University (VTU) \nBachelor of Engineering, Computer Science   \n \n \n \n \n                                      August 2009 - July 2013 \n \nEXPERIENCE \nWipro \nSenior Product Manager & Practice Partner  \n \n \n \n \n                                  November 2023 - Present \nPlano, TX, USA \n• \nDirected AI strategy and GTM execution across Healthcare, Retail, Life Sciences, Telecom verticals using ML/DL, GenAI, Agentic AI, and \nknowledge intelligence platforms, driving ~$250M opportunity pipeline and ~$50M+ in closed revenue. \n• \nPartnered with C-Suite leadership to build enterprise AI modernization roadmaps spanning clinical operations, regulatory workflows, \nand automation programs, aligning technology investments to measurable business outcomes and scalable value realization. \n• \nEstablished a large-scale AI Center of Excellence for a major U.S. healthcare payer leveraging GenAI, decision intelligence, and \nautomated workflows, reducing manual reviews by ~40%, improving claim turnaround by 25–30%, and delivering $50M+ annual cost \nefficiencies. \n• \nArchitected behavioral claims audit automation with Multi Agent System using Azure, Langchain stack across 5M+ annual claims, \nenabling real-time fraud and compliance anomaly detection and reducing manual intervention while increasing audit accuracy and \noperational assurance. \n• \nBuilt an enterprise Agentic AI system and workflow orchestration POC on Azure/Autogen stack to automate plan build and onboarding \nprocesses, cutting configuration cycles by 60%. \n• \nD