ion for medical applications (mastery of CNNs, Vision Transformers, GANs, segmentation, classification, explainable AI)\n• Hands-on proficiency: Python, TensorFlow/PyTorch, Pandas, scikit-learn, Azure ML (strongly preferred), Docker, REST APIs\n• Demonstrated success deploying AI in regulated medical devices (FDA 510(k), CE marking experience required)\n• Strong knowledge of FDA Good ML Practices, EU AI Act (high-risk AI requirements), data privacy (GDPR/HIPAA), and quality standards (ISO 13485, IEC 62304)\n• Track record of patents, peer-reviewed publications, or technical leadership in AI/healthcare\n• Experience leading cross-functional teams in a fast-paced, founder-driven organization\n\n\nPersonal Attributes (Non-Negotiable)\n\n• Extreme ownership — full accountability for outcomes, risks, and results\n• Bias for action in ambiguous, high-pressure situations; ability to juggle multiple complex initiatives without dropping quality\n• Outstanding influence without authority — build strong alignment across clinical, regulatory, engineering, and executive stakeholders\n• Rapid, independent learner who masters new domains and technologies quickly\n• Comfortable thriving in a high-expectation, direct-feedback, senior-leadership environment\n• Genuine passion for leveraging AI to prevent blindness and advance health equity globally\n\n\nIf you are a proven AI leader who blends world-class technical depth, clinical/regulatory acumen, and the drive to create meaningful global impact — we want to hear from you.\n\n\nJoin Remidio and help build the future of intelligent, accessible eye care that reaches every corner of the world.\n\n\n\n\n        Resume Content:\n        PAVAN HARESH \n+1 214-430-6317| paven026@gmail.com| linkedin.com/in/impavan/| Texas| USA(Open to Relocate) \n \nPROFESSIONAL SUMMARY \nAI Strategy and Enterprise Transformation Leader with 12+ years of experience driving large-scale AI adoption, product innovation, and \nmeasurable enterprise value acros