2026-01-14 19:22:55,152 - DEBUG - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/openai/v1/chat/completions', 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-f5450541-cdba-4924-bd50-f4097377afe3', 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': '\n        You are an expert Resume ATS Scanner and Career Coach. I want you to step-by-step analyze the resume against the job description to provide the most accurate optimization.\n\n        ### STEP-BY-STEP REASONING PROCESS:\n        1. **Analyze the JD**: First, identify the core hard skills, soft skills, and domain-specific tools required.\n        2. **Analyze the Resume**: Look for where these skills appear or are missing in the resume. Note any weak or generic language.\n        3. **Gap Analysis**: Compare the two. Where is the candidate strong? Where are the fatal flaws (missing keywords)? What specific metrics could be inferred or suggested to improve credibility?\n        4. **Formulate Recommendations**: For every weak point identified, draft a rewrite that strictly mimics the high-impact style of top-tier resumes (Action Verb + Task + Result/Metric).\n        5. **Final Output Generation**: Structure your findings into the requested JSON format.\n\n        ### INPUT DATA:\n        Job Description:\n        About the job\nJob Title: Head of Artificial Intelligence\nCompany: Remidio Innovative Solutions Pvt. Ltd.\nLocation: Peenya, Bangalore (Full-time, Work from Office)\nReporting to: Chief Medical Officer\nExperience Level: 10+ years (8+ years strongly preferred)\nEducation: Master’s or PhD in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, Mathematics, or a closely related field\n\n\nAbout Remidio\n\nRemidio is a fast-growing, global medtech innovator on a mission to prevent blindness through accessible, high-quality eye care. Our portable, FDA-cleared and CE-marked retinal imaging devices — powered by offline/edge AI — have already screened over 16 million patients across 55+ countries. We are revolutionizing population-scale screening for diabetic retinopathy, retinopathy of prematurity (ROP), glaucoma, AMD, and other blinding conditions by delivering intelligent, point-of-care diagnostics that are simple, affordable, and inclusive.\n\n\nWe are seeking a visionary, hands-on Head of Artificial Intelligence to own and accelerate our AI strategy, delivering clinically validated, regulatorily compliant innovations that transform global eye health and earn deep physician trust.\n\n\nRole Overview\n\n\n\nAs Head of Artificial Intelligence, you will be the strategic and technical leader for Remidio’s entire AI function. You will have end-to-end ownership of the AI vision, multi-year roadmap, model development, clinical validation, regulatory compliance, and worldwide scalability.\nThis is a high-impact, hands-on leadership role requiring deep expertise in medical computer vision, tight collaboration with clinical, regulatory, product, engineering, and founder teams, and the ability to ship production-grade AI that meets the highest global healthcare standards (FDA, CE, EU AI Act, etc.).\n\n\nYour leadership will directly shape the future of intelligent ophthalmic diagnostics and help Remidio reach millions more patients in underserved communities around the world.\n\n\nKey Responsibilities\n\n\n\n1. AI Strategy & Vision\n\n• Define and own Remidio’s long-term AI vision, multi-year roadmap, and technical strategy — aligned with clinical priorities, product goals, and business growth\n• Identify and integrate cutting-edge AI advancements (foundation models, multimodal AI, edge-optimized inference, etc.) into our portable retinal imaging ecosystem\n• Stay ahead of industry trends and convert emerging technologies into compliant, scalable, market-leading features\n2. End-to-End AI Development & Execution\n\n• Lead the full AI/ML lifecycle: data strategy & acquisition, model design, training, validation, deployment, monitoring, and lifecycle management\n• Build and advance state-of-the-art computer vision models (CNNs, Vision Transformers, GANs, self-supervised learning, segmentation, etc.) optimized for edge/offline use in medical devices\n• Drive production deployments in partnership with software engineering (web, desktop, mobile, cloud)\n3. Regulatory, Quality & Compliance Leadership\n\n• Own the AI regulatory strategy and serve as the primary AI subject-matter expert for FDA, CE, and other global submissions/audits\n• Ensure complete traceability, design controls, post-market surveillance, model drift management, and compliance with FDA Good Machine Learning Practice, EU AI Act (high-risk systems), ISO 13485, IEC 62304, and ISO 27001\n• Lead preparation of robust technical documentation and performance evidence for successful regulatory approvals\n4. Clinical Collaboration & Evidence Generation\n\n• Partner closely with clinical teams to design/execute AI validation studies, clinical performance evaluations, and real-world evidence generation\n• Guide data acquisition strategies to build diverse, high-quality, ethically sourced datasets for training, testing, and validation\n• Contribute to peer-reviewed publications, white papers, and scientific presentations\n5. Team Leadership & Culture Building\n\n• Recruit, mentor, and grow a world-class AI/ML engineering team (expand capability from current size to best-in-class)\n• Cultivate a culture of scientific excellence, rapid iteration, accountability, and unwavering focus on patient impact\n6. IP, Thought Leadership & External Impact\n\n• Proactively identify patentable innovations and drive the patent filing process\n• Strengthen Remidio’s external credibility through publications, conference speaking, and collaborations with academia, clinicians, and industry leaders\n\n\nMust-Have Qualifications & Experience\n\n• Proven track record in healthcare/medtech AI (ophthalmology, medical imaging, or diagnostics strongly preferred)\n• Deep expertise in Computer Vision for medical applications (mastery of CNNs, Vision Transformers, GANs, segmentation, classification, explainable AI)\n• Hands-on proficiency: Python, TensorFlow/PyTorch, Pandas, scikit-learn, Azure ML (strongly preferred), Docker, REST APIs\n• Demonstrated success deploying AI in regulated medical devices (FDA 510(k), CE marking experience required)\n• Strong knowledge of FDA Good ML Practices, EU AI Act (high-risk AI requirements), data privacy (GDPR/HIPAA), and quality standards (ISO 13485, IEC 62304)\n• Track record of patents, peer-reviewed publications, or technical leadership in AI/healthcare\n• Experience leading cross-functional teams in a fast-paced, founder-driven organization\n\n\nPersonal Attributes (Non-Negotiable)\n\n• Extreme ownership — full accountability for outcomes, risks, and results\n• Bias for action in ambiguous, high-pressure situations; ability to juggle multiple complex initiatives without dropping quality\n• Outstanding influence without authority — build strong alignment across clinical, regulatory, engineering, and executive stakeholders\n• Rapid, independent learner who masters new domains and technologies quickly\n• Comfortable thriving in a high-expectation, direct-feedback, senior-leadership environment\n• Genuine passion for leveraging AI to prevent blindness and advance health equity globally\n\n\nIf you are a proven AI leader who blends world-class technical depth, clinical/regulatory acumen, and the drive to create meaningful global impact — we want to hear from you.\n\n\nJoin Remidio and help build the future of intelligent, accessible eye care that reaches every corner of the world.\n\n\n\n\n        Resume Content:\n        PAVAN HARESH \n+1 214-430-6317| paven026@gmail.com| linkedin.com/in/impavan/| Texas| USA(Open to Relocate) \n \nPROFESSIONAL SUMMARY \nAI Strategy and Enterprise Transformation Leader with 12+ years of experience driving large-scale AI adoption, product innovation, and \nmeasurable enterprise value across Healthcare, Retail, BFSI, and Energy verticals and cross industry functions such as F&A, HR, Procurement, \nlegal, marketing, Supply Chain. Proven commercial and delivery track record generating $250M+ pipeline, closing $50M+ revenue, and enabling \n$1B+ in business impact through AI modernization, platform development, and GTM execution. Deep expertise in Generative AI, Agentic AI, RAG \necosystems, Conversational AI, Knowledge Intelligence, and enterprise AI platforms across Azure, AWS, and Google Cloud combining hands-on \ntechnical credibility with strong product leadership and C-Suite partnership. Recognized for building scalable AI platforms, establishing \nresponsible AI governance in regulated environments, and leading cross-functional engineering, data, and product teams to deliver secure, \ncompliant, and high-impact AI solutions at enterprise scale. \n \nEDUCATION \nVisvesvaraya Technological University (VTU) \nBachelor of Engineering, Computer Science   \n \n \n \n \n                                      August 2009 - July 2013 \n \nEXPERIENCE \nWipro \nSenior Product Manager & Practice Partner  \n \n \n \n \n                                  November 2023 - Present \nPlano, TX, USA \n• \nDirected AI strategy and GTM execution across Healthcare, Retail, Life Sciences, Telecom verticals using ML/DL, GenAI, Agentic AI, and \nknowledge intelligence platforms, driving ~$250M opportunity pipeline and ~$50M+ in closed revenue. \n• \nPartnered with C-Suite leadership to build enterprise AI modernization roadmaps spanning clinical operations, regulatory workflows, \nand automation programs, aligning technology investments to measurable business outcomes and scalable value realization. \n• \nEstablished a large-scale AI Center of Excellence for a major U.S. healthcare payer leveraging GenAI, decision intelligence, and \nautomated workflows, reducing manual reviews by ~40%, improving claim turnaround by 25–30%, and delivering $50M+ annual cost \nefficiencies. \n• \nArchitected behavioral claims audit automation with Multi Agent System using Azure, Langchain stack across 5M+ annual claims, \nenabling real-time fraud and compliance anomaly detection and reducing manual intervention while increasing audit accuracy and \noperational assurance. \n• \nBuilt an enterprise Agentic AI system and workflow orchestration POC on Azure/Autogen stack to automate plan build and onboarding \nprocesses, cutting configuration cycles by 60%. \n• \nDesigned GenAI SOP conversational agent on Azure to find accurate answers from relevant SOP clauses, enhancing Dental First pass \nand adjustments claims processor\'s efficiency by 30%. \nProduct Manager \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n                      February 2022 - November 2023 \nLondon, UK \n• \nOwned global product roadmap and delivery for AI-powered Knowledge Platforms built using Azure Cognitive Search (BM25 + \nSemantic + Hybrid Search), indexing 80M+ documents across 12TB of enterprise content and improving knowledge access and \ndecisioning for ENU client. \n• \nLed agile delivery as Product Manager and Scrum Master, managing sprints, stakeholder priorities, and platform enhancements to \nensure predictable delivery, product adoption, and measurable business outcomes. \n• \nOversaw enterprise migration from Apache Solr to Azure Cognitive Search, enhancing scalability, search results relevancy and \naccuracy, improving search efficiency and operational resilience. \n• \nDefined and executed responsible AI governance practices aligned to regulatory frameworks, ensuring secure, compliant, and risk-\naware AI adoption. \n• \nAdvanced GTM execution for AI offerings in regulated industries, guiding customers from PoC to full enterprise rollout, driving tangible \nROI and operational modernization. \n \nSolution Architect \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n        August 2019 - February 2022 \nBengaluru, India \n• \nDesigned and implemented end-to-end architecture and delivery of Contact Center Transformation and Knowledge Intelligence \nplatforms on Azure, aligning technical solutions to business goals, scalability requirements, and security standards for Manufacturing \nand Telecom clients in UK geo. \n• \nArchitected migration of Conversational AI platforms from IBM Cloud to Azure using NLP frameworks and cloud re-engineering, \nimproving reliability, performance, and cost efficiency with minimal downtime. \n• \nCollaborated with business, vendor, and technical stakeholders to define architecture blueprints, delivery plans, and execution \ngovernance, ensuring program stability, stakeholder alignment, and successful deployment. \n \n \n \nUniphore \nSenior Software Engineer  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n                         November 2018 - August 2019 \nBengaluru, India \n• \nBuilt advanced NLP and conversational AI solutions for healthcare client using deep learning (Bi-LSTM, entity extraction) deployed in \nsecure cloud environments, enabling automation, improved service quality, and operational efficiency. \n• \nLed secure deployment and lifecycle management of ML/DL models, ensuring reliability, compliance, and sustained performance. \nPlankton Solutions \nSenior Software Engineer \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n          June 2016 - November 2018 \nBengaluru, India \n• \nDesigned and deployed enterprise chatbot and analytics platforms using AI/ML and AWS cloud infrastructure, enhancing customer \nexperience and operational intelligence. \n• \nLed presales engineering, client solution design, and analytics delivery, supporting successful client adoption and market-\naligned AI deployment. \nTech Mahindra \nSenior Project Engineer \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n               January 2014 - June 2016 \nBengaluru, India \n• \nDelivered enterprise automation solutions across QA, UI, and reporting for Fortune 500 clients using Python, Selenium, Appium tools, \nimproving operational efficiency, stability, and risk governance. \n \nCERTIFICATION \n• \nAgentic AI - DeepLearning.AI \n• \nGen